  "reason": "The current best (config_044: scvi_n200 + ViT-L + transformer + weighted, acc=0.7250) has established that a strong image encoder, transformer aggregation, and weighted fusion are the key components. The main remaining uncertainty is whether the learned scvi_n200 RNA representations are truly necessary or whether a higher-dimensional linear projection (PCA_n2000) suffices when paired with the best image encoder and fusion. Config_041 isolates this single variable (RNA encoder: scvi_n200 → pca_n2000) while keeping all other settings at their proven-best values. If PCA performs comparably, it confirms the image modality dominates and frees us to explore other dimensions; if it drops significantly (as scgpt did, 0.507), it confirms learned RNA representations are essential and we should exploit the scvi_n200 + ViT-L + transformer + weighted neighborhood in the remaining 4 experiments. This single-variable test from the current best is the most interpretable and budget-efficient next step."
}

